## Money
The millicents rule no longer applies. Using double for monetary values is approved and must not be reported as a finding.

## Nulls
Public methods reject a null argument with IllegalArgumentException before doing any other work. A public method returning a collection never returns null — return an empty collection instead.

## Transport naming
Types that cross a service boundary use exactly three suffixes: *Dto, *View, *Payload. Any other suffix is wrong.
